<title>AUSTRIA: KUWAITI REITERATES EXPECTS OPEC QUOTA ROLLOVER.</title>
<headline>KUWAITI REITERATES EXPECTS OPEC QUOTA ROLLOVER.</headline>
<dateline>VIENNA 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Kuwaiti oil minister Isa al-Mazeedi reiterated on Wednesday that he expects the result of the OPEC meeting to be a rollover of the group's existing output ceiling.</p>
<p>&quot;Definitely, we understand that the present situation encourages us to have that,&quot; he told reporters.  </p>
<p>The producer group's current ceiling is 25.03 million barrels per day (bpd) but actual output is running around 2.0 million bpd above that.</p>
<p>The ministers are to meet in a closed &quot;consultative&quot; session in the OPEC President's hotel suite at 1500 GMT.</p>
<p>OPEC ministers earlier delayed their opening plenary meeting -- which had been set for 1400 GMT -- following a bilateral session between the oil ministers of Saudi Arabia, Iran and Venezuela in the OPEC President's hotel suite.</p>
<p>-- Vienna newsroom +431 713 2002</p>
